            subj: 'Confused, remembers nothing of the event. Headache, sore tongue and aching muscles. Drowsy.',
            assess: `Two generalized tonic-clonic seizures (the second in the ED, treated with lorazepam 2 mg IV). Post-ictal lactic acidosis (lactate 5.2); glucose normal. ${known ? 'Subtherapeutic due to missed doses.' : 'No provoking factor yet; CT head, EEG and MRI planned.'}`,
            plan: ['Airway, side-lying, oxygen; lorazepam IV for seizure over 5 minutes; keep suction at bedside.', usePhe ? 'Fosphenytoin load with ECG/BP monitoring and phenytoin level (levetiracetam avoided with depression history).' : 'Levetiracetam IV load then maintenance; switch to oral when alert.', 'Glucose, Na, Ca, Mg, lactate, CK, toxicology, ethanol, pregnancy test (if applicable); CT head now; MRI and EEG.', 'NPO until awake and swallow screen; seizure and aspiration precautions; neuro checks.', 'Neurology consult.'],
            nursing: ['GCS 13, oriented to person only; follows commands; seizure precautions in place with padded rails and suction at bedside.', 'Brief second seizure in the ED treated with lorazepam; SpO2 92% then 97% on 2 L; now post-ictal, side-lying.', 'Tongue laceration: oral care with swab; NPO until alert.', 'Neuro checks hourly; glucose 112 mg/dL.'],
            teach: ['Family told what a seizure is and what to do (time it, side-lying, nothing in the mouth) and why NPO and rails are used.'],
            dispo: 'Anticipate 1-3 days; discharge when seizure-free, on oral antiepileptic, with safety teaching.',
